@@ -69,3 +69,15 @@ Tests include real parent/iframe checkpoints, five-question grading, actual heal
 ## Release 2.1.2: Ground summoning circle
 
 Cast places a detailed SVG inscription on the floor: concentric engraved rings, varied runes, cardinal anchors and a geometric central sigil. The boundary matches the spell’s reach and stays fixed while the inner rune bands counter-rotate. Scenery and combat actors render above the cast and its circular detonation. Reduced motion freezes the rune animation.
+
+## Release 2.2.0: Student beta and premium presentation
+
+Etched stonework, animated pillar lights, orbiting reward-gate rings, spectral dash silhouettes and metallic menu treatments add depth without changing combat hitboxes. Cosmetic work is bounded; environmental animation uses simulation time and freezes with reduced motion.
+
+Hades is available to signed-in students in Science and Math with the BETA label retained. Student rounds use the active learner’s school level and separate account history; administrators retain level-selectable previews. Science records bank attempts through its existing game history. Math top-level MCQs are marked by the portal’s existing authenticated `markAttempt` service: private keys are never loaded by the student client or sent to the iframe. Existing block MCQs remain parent-graded. Failed, stale or malformed remote results cannot advance a sanctuary round.
+
+## Release 2.2.1: Precise casting and combat feedback
+
+Q/E captures the floor beneath the mouse or pen cursor immediately, even after camera movement, screen shake, layout scaling or resizing. Moving or aiming afterward leaves the summoning circle at that world position; pressing Cast again detonates it. Keyboard-only and touch players keep assisted aim.
+
+Desktop and touch ability indicators show cast lifetime and detonation availability, low Magick, strike/special/dash cooldowns and Hex charge. Doom now resolves during sustained attacks, Chill pulses keep consistent timing and preserve longer freezes, Blizzard pulls respect pillars, and dash travel and knockback follow the actual movement direction. Existing premium presentation and parent-owned learning integrations remain included in the source used to reproduce the portal builds.
